Q: How to know if a connection with a shared worker is still alive? A: <p>A nice solution <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/LockManager" rel="nofollow noreferrer">using locks</a> is discussed in the <a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1766#issuecomment-633197720" rel="nofollow noreferrer">whatwg github issue</a> and is <a href="https://caniuse.com/mdn-api_lock" rel="nofollow noreferrer">widely available</a>:</p>
<pre><code>/// worker
const lockReqId = 'process-live-'+Date.now()+Math.random();
navigator.locks.request(lockReqId,()=&gt;new Promise(()=&gt;{}));
postMessage(lockReqId);

/// master
worker.addEventListener('message', me=&gt;{
  if(typeof me.data==='string' &amp;&amp; me.data.startsWith(&quot;process-live-&quot;)){
    navigator.locks.request(me.data,()=&gt;{
      worker.dispatchEvent(new CloseEvent('close'))
    })
  }
});
</code></pre>

Q: Svelte Layerchart - Formatting Axis Data A: <p>There's a <code>scaleToFit</code> option inside <code>tickLabelProps</code>.<br />
So one of the solutions is to increase the width and set <code>scaleToFit</code> to <code>true</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>    &lt;LineChart
        data={someData}
        x=&quot;name&quot;
        y=&quot;value&quot;
        props={{
            spline: {
                curve: curveLinearClosed,
                class: &quot;stroke-primary fill-primary/20&quot;
            },
            xAxis: {
                tickLength: 10,
                // HERE:
                tickLabelProps: {
                    width: 75,
                    scaleToFit: true,
                    textAnchor: &quot;middle&quot;
                }
            },
            yAxis: {
                // ...

            }
            // ...

    /&gt;
</code></pre>
